| Bitbucket on the Work pages (#3786): **Work ▸ Issues** and **Pull requests** list the issues and pull requests of the folders on bitbucket.org with the Bitbucket connection (#3785), a call per repository with a BBQL filter, merged by when they changed; an item's page reads its body, comments (newest page first), and a pull request's commit statuses (each with its Pipelines run), participants' reviews, diffstat (files changed, conflicts) and the target branch's merge strategies; the writes are comment, an issue's kind and component as its labels, close (resolve) and reopen, decline, merge (merge, squash or rebase-fast-forward, as the branch allows, at the head the page shows), approve, rerun (each failed Pipelines run, every step), a check's log and the diff | Mac, web, Remote | built, walked on a fake Bitbucket | — | 2026-11-07, against a stand-in Bitbucket over HTTP (`Go/internal/bitbucketmcp/forge_test.go`, `Go/internal/agentsd/forgebitbucket_test.go`) and on a scratch app with a fake Bitbucket over HTTP (the Mac window and the web page) | `Go/internal/bitbucketmcp/forge.go`, `Go/internal/bitbucketmcp/forgewrite.go`, `Go/internal/agentsd/forgebitbucket.go` | not yet on a real workspace (Alex's test, #3771): the BBQL filters (`updated_on<=`, `~`, `component.name`), the comments' `size`, a pull request's `participants`, a branch's `merge_strategies`, `PUT` on an issue and the diff's redirect are unproven on Bitbucket Cloud; no merge when checks pass or reopen of a declined pull request (Bitbucket has neither); a pull request has no labels; no plan or boards (Bitbucket has no sub-issues, dependencies or boards); Work ▸ Features (#3880): a `feature:<name>` component is the issue's feature, with no epics |
